Where did you read that?  Surely that's not correct 
in nethack.  If you refer to the spoiler at

http://www.spod-central.org/~psmith/nh/food-343.txt 

the formulation there 

| Turn 4 of 20   Ring worn on left hand (except a +0 ring).
| Turn 12 of 20  Ring worn on right hand (except a +0 ring).

means (if I understand correctly) that each ring gives 
one additional nutrition loss each 20 turns, the difference 
being when.  On left hand, you'll lose the point on moves 
4, 24, 44, 64, 84, .., on right hand, it would be 12,32,52,..

> So where should I wear my ring of slow digestion? 

If you have one, it shouldn't matter.  It prevents the usual 
hunger, but not the ring--induced one.  If you happen to have 
two rings, here's an untested idea, just from reading the 
spoiler:  Start with wearing both rings. 

1) On turn n*20 + 3, slip off the ring on left hand.  
2) On turn n*20 + 10, put the ring on left hand on again. 
3) On turn n*20 + 11, slip off the ring on right hand. 
4) On turn (n+1)*20 + 2, put the ring on right hand on again. 
5) Repeat.  

This will become boring like hell, but unless you wear an 
amulet or carry the AoY, you should be able to run without 
getting hungry forever.  (With one ring, it doesn't work since 
the slip--off--put--on combo would require one round unprotected 
from nutrition loss.)  Again, it's untested, but if I understood 
the spoiler correctly, it should work.  

Actually, if it works, this would be a way to make a 
foodless polyselfless atheist ascension in a slightly 
different manner than the ones I've read about; if one 
extends the above series by 

3a) On turn n*20 + 15, drop the AoY, 
3b) On turn n*20 + 17, pick up the AoY, 

you might even get away with it while carrying the AoY.  
(Of course, similar for worn amulets, but it starts to 
become a bit ridicolous then.)   Hence, it may be that, 
in theory, you could ascend !food, !god, !polyself, !wishes 
without even drinking one potion of fruit juice, although 
that would require quite some luck in the beginning, and a bit 
of luck at astral plane (famine..)  Feel free to try, though ;-). 

